sclaim and the served-path table    | dials and reads; a closed connection is observed as the      |               |\ndocs/design/dao.stream.remote.implementation-plan.md:98:|    | with `serve-step`, `step`, `driver` (clj), `async`;         | module; `dao.space.index`, btree hydration, the linker M3    |               |\ndocs/design/dao.stream.remote.implementation-plan.md:103:| 5  | REPL as a service: `yin.repl.serve` and `connect` over     | `(connect \"daostream:ws://...\")` resolves to a remote        | clj cljs cljd |\ndocs/design/dao.stream.remote.implementation-plan.md:104:|    | `requests` and `answers` reflections; delete               | descriptor pair; the demo REPLs work; `yin.repl.link` serves |               |\ndocs/design/dao.stream.remote.implementation-plan.md:106:|    | envelope from `dao.stream.apply`; rework or retire         | reflections or retired in the same slice, because the apply  |               |\ndocs/design/dao.stream.remote.implementation-plan.md:111:|    | `src/clj/dao/stream/udp/jvm.clj`, `src/cljs/dao/           | oversize beyond the maximum answers `transport-error`        |               |\ndocs/design/dao.stream.remote.implementation-plan.md:117:|    |                                                            | tolerance; a reconnect within it finds the pair intact; a    |               |\ndocs/design/dao.stream.remote.implementation-plan.md:144:- `dao.lease.md` (done): served entries and relay pairs named as lease\ndocs/design/dao.stream.remote.implementation-plan.md:175:  own Close-section \"server-side accepted-connection handle\", track the\ndocs/design/dao.stream.remote.implementation-plan.md:185:  projection. Its accept and disclaim frames and served-path table become\ndocs/design/dao.stream.remote.implementation-plan.md:188:- `dao.stream.serving`: **retired**. Forwards a source into every accepted\ndocs/design/dao.stream.remote.implementation-plan.md:190:  consumers are `yin.repl.serve` and `dao.jing.remote` (which requires and\ndocs/design/dao.stream.remote.implementation-plan.md:191:  drives it); both are retired by slices 4 and 5.\ndocs/design/dao.stream.remote.implementation-plan.md:196:  such vocabulary over reflections, or retired in slice 5.\ndocs/design/dao.stream.remote.implementation-plan.md:197:- `dao.stream.rpc.ws`: **retired**. Its only job is translating `:ws/`\ndocs/design/dao.stream.remote.implementation-plan.md:199:- `dao.stream.apply` as a wire envelope: **retired**. Its ok-or-error\ndocs/design/dao.stream.remote.implementation-plan.md:200:  wrapper duplicates the outcome map. The `:dao.stream.apply/call` AST node\ndocs/design/dao.stream.remote.implementation-plan.md:202:- `yin.repl.serve`, `connect`, `driver`, `adapter`, the `daostream:ws://`\ndocs/design/dao.stream.remote.implementation-plan.md:207:  coordinate in `dao.jing.coordinate`: **retired**. Deprecated whole;\ncollab/1790497441896-vm-engineer-dao-stream-remote-slice5.r4.claude.findings.md:4:**Done: the Architect's lease-sketch ruling, applied.** `test/dao/lease_composition_test.cljc` no longer requires `dao.stream.serving`/`dao.stream.ws`. `served-connection-real-close-path-sketch-test` and the `serving-fixture`/`ws-admission`/`handoff-admission`/`served-descriptor`/`buffer` private helpers it alone used are gone. In their place, `served-entry-reclaim-through-reflection-test` drives a real `dao.stream.remote` mirror table and holder reflection over two in-process ring buffers as the channel, with a separate per-author renewal medium wired to the judge exactly as the ruling specifies: initial-tick resolve-and-read, a renewal counted at reading 7, idempotent reclaim at reading 18 (table entry removed, exactly one `(lease/lapsed L :silence)` on the writer, ledger cleared), then one more reflection request answered `:dao.stream.remote/not-found`, confirmed on a subsequent op too. The separate carriage sketch (`served-connection-lifetime-sketch-test`, its grant/`:lapsed` assertions) is untouched, per the ruling. Full JVM suite: 2,279 tests / 183,285 assertions / 0 failures — the count shift from baseline is this rewrite, not a regression.\ncollab/1790497441896-vm-engineer-dao-stream-remote-slice5.r4.claude.findings.md:6:**Blocked on the remainder.** Reconnaissance for the rest of slice 5 (rewriting `yin.repl.serve`/`connect` onto reflections, deleting `dao.stream.serving` and `dao.stream.rpc.ws`, retiring the apply wire envelope, and the deferred `dao.stream.ws` retirements) surfaced a second tree/plan conflict, distinct from the lease-sketch one, that step 3 of the brief (\"retire the apply wire envelope from `dao.stream.apply`... the AST node and FFI bridge keep the name\") does not authorize me to resolve alone:\ncollab/1790497441896-vm-engineer-dao-stream-remote-slice5.r4.claude.findings.md:8:`src/cljc/yin/vm/ffi.cljc` and `src/cljc/yin/vm/ast_walker.cljc` (`:require [dao.stream.apply :as apply2]`) call `apply2/request`, `apply2/response?`, `apply2/response-id`, `apply2/response-ok`, `apply2/response-error`, `apply2/put-request!`, `apply2/put-response!`, and `apply2/dispatch-request` — the *entire* function surface of `dao.stream.apply.cljc`, not just the `:dao.stream.apply/call` AST-node keyword the plan names as unrelated-and-kept. This is the VM's own FFI-call bridge, unrelated to REPL networking, and it is a load-bearing consumer: deleting `dao.stream.apply.cljc` as literally instructed breaks core VM evaluation, not just the network path. The earlier reconnaissance round that concluded \"moving the envelope into `dao.stream.rpc.cljc` before deleting `dao.stream.apply.cljc`\" never checked this consumer.\ncollab/1790497441896-vm-engineer-dao-stream-remote-slice5.r4.claude.findings.md:10:The resolution I can see, but shouldn't apply unilaterally under the same \"no backward-compat shims\" / scope-authority rule that gated the lease-sketch case: **keep `dao.stream.apply.cljc` exactly as-is** (it stays the FFI bridge's envelope, untouched) and read \"retire the apply wire envelope\" as retiring it *as the REPL's network wire format specifically* — satisfied by deleting `dao.stream.rpc.ws.cljc` (its only job, translating `:ws/...` frames, is gone once reflections deliver raw values with no envelope wrapping) and `dao.stream.serving.cljc`, and by a small, additive rework inside `dao.stream.rpc.cljc` (only consumed by `yin.repl.driver`/`adapter`/`connect`, confirmed by grep) to translate a reflection's `:dao.stream/transport-error` + `:dao.stream.remote/reason` (`:not-found`, `:channel-gone`) and bare `:dao.stream/end` into the existing `:dao.stream.apply/not-found`, `/detached`, `/ended` terminal values `driver.cljc`'s `reattachable?` already keys on — with no change to `dao.stream.apply.cljc` or to `yin.vm.ffi`/`ast_walker` at all. `yin.repl.serve`/`connect` would then compose directly over `dao.stream.remote`/`dao.stream.ws-project` (`dial`/`dial-attach!`/`make-acceptor`/`accept-step!`, both proven in slice 3) for two identities, `\"yin.repl/requests\"` and `\"yin.repl/answers\"`, with the server's own step reusing the existing `evaluate`/incomplete-input logic already in `serve.cljc` against one shared queue instead of a per-attachment session pool — collapsing rather than growing that module. This also confirmed the ws.cljc retirement's scope: `:served`/disclaim (`ws.cljc:494-502`) and the `:ws/accept` frame send (`ws.cljc:556-570`) are exactly the debt named, now redundant with the mirror's own per-identity `not-found`.\ncollab/1790497441896-vm-engineer-dao-stream-remote-slice5.r4.claude.findings.md:12:I did not start editing `yin.repl.serve.cljc`, `connect.cljc`, `dao.stream.rpc.cljc`, or `dao.stream.ws.cljc` pending that ruling — the tree outside the lease-composition test is unchanged.\ncollab/1790497441896-vm-engineer-dao-stream-remote-slice5.r4.claude.findings.md:14:Status: BLOCKED - dao.stream.apply.cljc is a load-bearing dependency of yin.vm.ffi.cljc/yin.vm.ast_walker.cljc (the VM's FFI bridge, out of this slice's s